    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `capacityWarning` to flag when an owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), leaving the existing 50-owner rejection untouched.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I added behaviour as a new cohesive unit rather than growing any existing method:\n\n1. **New `FlagCapacityWarning.java`** (single-method class, WMC_other = 0) \u2014 mirrors the existing `FlagBulkSignup` pattern and *reuses* `CheckCityCapacity.normalize` and `CheckCityCapacity.CAPACITY` instead of duplicating the city-count/normalization logic. Sets `capacityWarning` true when `40 \u2264 count < 50`.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient capacityWarning` field plus its `isCapacityWarning`/`setCapacityWarning` accessors (new methods; no existing method changed).\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name convention (no mapper change needed).\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `flagCapacityWarning` step right after `checkCityCapacity` (one existing `next:` line retargeted).\n\nI did not touch `OwnerMapper`, the repository, or any other function \u2014 the mapper picks up the field automatically.\n\nResult: `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` passes and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
